# Secure Coding Standards — {{workspace_or_stack_title}}

Use this skill when writing or reviewing code that touches untrusted input, authentication, authorization, data scopes, secrets, sensitive data/PII, outbound calls, file handling, or third-party dependencies.

---

## 1. Deterministic Security Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

Run these checks on touched files before handoff or review. Each gate produces a binary **`PASS`** or **`FAIL`** status (or `NOT_RUN` with an explicit blocker reason—never `PASS` when unrun):

| Check | Command / Tool | Gate Status |
|---|---|---|
| **Static Security Linter** | `{{security_linter_cmd}}` | `PASS` / `FAIL` |
| **Hardcoded Secrets Audit (`rg`)** | `{{rg_secrets_audit_cmd}}` (expect 0 matches) | `PASS` / `FAIL` |
| **Injection & Transport Bypass Audit (`rg`)** | `{{rg_injection_or_tls_audit_cmd}}` (expect 0 matches) | `PASS` / `FAIL` |
| **Sensitive Logging Audit (`rg`)** | `{{rg_sensitive_logging_audit_cmd}}` (expect 0 matches) | `PASS` / `FAIL` |
| **Dependency & Lockfile Audit** | `{{dependency_audit_cmd}}` | `PASS` / `FAIL` |

---

## 2. Core Security Rules (`SC1`–`SC14` — Mandatory Compliance)

All 14 security rules are **mandatory compliance** when designing, writing, or modifying code. During Code Review, violations are graded on the unified 3-tier scale (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR` — see [03 — Runtime Risks, Dependencies & Review]({{ref_03}})):

| ID | Rule | Workspace Contract | Reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| **SC1** | **Validate Untrusted Input at the Boundary** | {{sc1_contract}} | [01 — Input, Auth & Data Scope]({{ref_01}}) |
| **SC2** | **Authorize Every Operation per Object** | {{sc2_contract}} | [01 — Input, Auth & Data Scope]({{ref_01}}) |
| **SC3** | **Isolate Data Scopes Explicitly** | {{sc3_contract}} | [01 — Input, Auth & Data Scope]({{ref_01}}) |
| **SC4** | **Prevent Injection Across Interpreters** | {{sc4_contract}} | [03 — Runtime Risks, Deps & Review]({{ref_03}}) |
| **SC5** | **Encode Output & Validate Navigation/Redirects** | {{sc5_contract}} | [01 — Input, Auth & Data Scope]({{ref_01}}), [03 — Runtime Risks, Deps & Review]({{ref_03}}) |
| **SC6** | **Keep Secrets Out of Source, Bundles & Logs** | {{sc6_contract}} | [02 — Secrets, Data & Crypto]({{ref_02}}) |
| **SC7** | **Use Verified Authentication & Session Lifecycles** | {{sc7_contract}} | [01 — Input, Auth & Data Scope]({{ref_01}}) |
| **SC8** | **Redact Sensitive Data & PII from Logs & Errors** | {{sc8_contract}} | [02 — Secrets, Data & Crypto]({{ref_02}}) |
| **SC9** | **Enforce Transport Security & Guard Outbound Calls** | {{sc9_contract}} | [03 — Runtime Risks, Deps & Review]({{ref_03}}) |
| **SC10** | **Handle Files & External Payloads Defensively** | {{sc10_contract}} | [03 — Runtime Risks, Deps & Review]({{ref_03}}) |
| **SC11** | **Vet Dependencies & Lock Supply Chain** | {{sc11_contract}} | [03 — Runtime Risks, Deps & Review]({{ref_03}}) |
| **SC12** | **Use Vetted Cryptography & Secure Randomness** | {{sc12_contract}} | [02 — Secrets, Data & Crypto]({{ref_02}}) |
| **SC13** | **Fail Closed on Security & Validation Errors** | {{sc13_contract}} | [01 — Input, Auth & Data Scope]({{ref_01}}), [03 — Runtime Risks, Deps & Review]({{ref_03}}) |
| **SC14** | **Flag Security-Sensitive Changes in Handoff** | {{sc14_contract}} | [03 — Runtime Risks, Deps & Review]({{ref_03}}) |

